Original commit body from bbe8290:

NestJS routes now correctly combine class-level @Controller('/users')
with method-level @Get(':id') to produce full paths like /users/:id.

Previously only the method decorator path was extracted, causing routes
to display as method descriptors (e.g., ":id") instead of full HTTP paths.

Changes:
- Add _get_enclosing_class_node() to walk up AST to class
- Add _get_class_route_prefix() to extract Controller decorator path
- Add _combine_route_paths() for path normalization
- Handle both exported and non-exported class patterns
- Add comprehensive tests for path combination edge cases

This pattern (class prefix + method path) also exists in Spring Boot
(@RequestMapping + @GetMapping) and ASP.NET ([Route] + [HttpGet]).
The generalized approach can be extended to Java/C# in future work.
